/** @page treesitter_release_notesguide Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section treesitter_v1_0 treesitter Module Version 1.0

    - Nodes and traversal/query cursors retain their underlying syntax trees after temporary or deleted tree
      objects are released. Copying a child preserves its complete source, and resetting a cursor updates
      both the syntax tree and source used by subsequent nodes.
    - Compile the installed Qore grammar's external scanner when present, fixing unresolved scanner symbols on macOS
      and enabling Qore brace-delimited regular expressions. Older grammars without a scanner remain supported.
    - Build the pinned Python and YAML grammars without unused-value warnings; source fixes are hash-checked
      and written only to the build tree, with unchanged scanner and lexer behavior.
    - Initial release with support for Python, Java, JSON, YAML, JavaScript (js), Kotlin (kt), TypeScript (ts), and
      TSX
    - Full tree-sitter API: parsing, tree traversal, cursors, and queries
    - Incremental parsing support
    - Query pattern matching for syntax highlighting and code analysis
*/
